  "query_preview": "/Wednesday through Sunday/...\nA Pacific trough will begin to move inland by mid week, nudging\nthe bulk of the monsoon moisture toward the east. Hot surface \ntemperatures and continued moist mid-levels will keep shower and\nthunderstorm chances for the higher terrain Wednesday and \nThursday, mainly over SW Idaho mountains. Models start to \nmishandle the propagation of the Pacific trough and moisture \nFriday into the weekend, leading to low forecast confidence of \nshowers/thunderstorms within the forecast area. Overall, slight \nchances linger over higher terrain as hot, south-southwest flow\nattempts to dominate through the weekend. Surface max temperatures\nshould remain 5-10 degrees above normal through the forecast \nperiod.",
